plaso-wifi.tsv and plaso-launchd.tsv.gz: what plaso (the
log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads from plaso's wifi.log,
wifi_turned_over.log and macos_launchd.log (tests/fixtures/plaso/, see its
NOTICE) with its text/mac_wifi and text/macos_launchd_log parsers, written
by gen_logs.py from psort's JSON lines: one line per event, sorted: the
file, the time, plaso's name for it, the parser, and every value plaso
read as name=value. tests/logs.rs compares them.

A Wi-Fi log has no years: plaso takes them from the file's times and the
current year, so the oracle depends on both. It was made on 2026-10-08,
on a Debian host with Docker, from a folder holding the logs as below
(each copy's change time is when it was copied, in 2026; a gzip file's
only time is the one in its header):

  mkdir -p in/old in/y2025 in/y2026 in/gz in/launchd
  cp wifi.log wifi_turned_over.log in/old/
  cp wifi.log in/y2025/; cp wifi.log in/y2026/; cp wifi.log in/gz/
  gzip -dc macos_launchd.log.gz > in/launchd/macos_launchd.log
  touch -d "2014-01-05 12:00:00" in/old/wifi.log
  touch -d "2017-01-03 12:00:00" in/old/wifi_turned_over.log
  touch -d "2025-06-01 12:00:00" in/y2025/wifi.log
  touch -d "2026-01-02 12:00:00" in/y2026/wifi.log
  touch -d "2025-06-01 12:00:00" in/gz/wifi.log && gzip -9 in/gz/wifi.log

  sudo docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/data" log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    log2timeline --status_view none -q \
    --parsers 'text/mac_wifi,text/macos_launchd_log' \
    --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
  sudo docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/data" log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    psort --status_view none -q -a -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso
  python3 -I gen_logs.py out.jsonl text/mac_wifi > plaso-wifi.tsv
  python3 -I gen_logs.py out.jsonl text/macos_launchd_log | gzip -9n > plaso-launchd.tsv.gz

(psort's -a keeps events it would drop as duplicates.) The other oracles'
commands are in the headers of gen.sh, gen_events.py and gen_usage.py.

btm.tsv: every item of the background items files (plaso's
backgrounditems.btm and tests/fixtures/puffycid/, see its NOTICE) as
Python's own plistlib, an NSKeyedArchiver resolver and a bookmark reader
written in gen_btm.py read them, independently of this crate. plaso's
macos_background_items_plist plugin (log2timeline/plaso:20260720) agrees
on every bookmark it reads: iTunesHelper and Syncthing, the two creation
times, volume name, mount point and flags. It reads the five other records
of BackgroundItems-v4.btm as empty events (no bookmark), and fails on
backgrounditemsPoisonApple.btm ("'list' object has no attribute 'get'":
its internalItems are an array, not an NSHashTable).

  cd tests/fixtures
  python3 -I ../oracle/gen_btm.py plaso/backgrounditems.btm \
    puffycid/backgrounditemsPoisonApple.btm puffycid/BackgroundItems-v4.btm \
    puffycid/BackgroundItems-v4-binary.btm > ../oracle/btm.tsv
